Data corresponding to the COHERENT Collaboration result shown in arXiv:1708.01294[nucl-ex]
Part of a release package including a descriptive document and code examples showing interaction with the data

The full release package can be found at http://coherent.ornl.gov/data. The example code can be found, on its own, at https://code.ornl.gov/COHERENT/codeExamples_dataRelease_april2018.

Note that the quenching factor (QF) data points are included for those who might want to develop their own parameterization of the QF, introducing (say) energy dependence.
The QF used for the analysis of the 2017 publication was an energy-independent value determined by global literature data.
The QF in the 2017 analysis is included in the YAML file.

For a full description, and the recommended way to cite this data, see the PDF document accompanying this release.

Files included here:
	data_anticoincidence_beamOff.txt: Data taken with NO SNS beam, representing the anti-coincidence (AC) region of the waveform where no neutrino events are expected.
	data_coincidence_beamOff.txt: Data taken with NO SNS beam, representing the coincidence (C) region of the waveform where neutrino and neutron events are expected to occur.
	data_anticoincidence_beamOn.txt: Data taken WITH SNS beam, representing the AC region. This would generally be considered the background region.
	data_coincidence_beamOn.txt: Data taken WITH SNS beam, representing the C region. This would generally be considered the signal region.
	
	arrivalTimePDF_promptNeutrons.txt: Data describing the arrival-time distribution of signals associated with prompt neutrons. Overall normalization effectively arbitrary.
	arrivalTimePDF_promptNeutrinos.txt: Data describing the arrival-time distribution of signals associated with the prompt neutrino population (i.e., muon neutrinos from pion decay). Overall normalization effectively arbitrary.
	arrivalTimePDF_delayedNeutrinos.txt: Data describing the arrival-time distribution of signals associated with the delayed neutrino population (i.e., anti-muon and electron neutrinos from muon decay). Overall normalization effectively arbitrary.	

	promptPDF.txt: Distribution of the expected number of events from prompt, SNS-produced neutrons in photoelectron space per gigawatt-hour of SNS beam exposure. No analysis efficiency is applied in advance to this data, and this must be done by the user.
	
	qfData_chicago.txt: CsI-Na quenching factor data points from Chicago experiment shown in publication. 
	qfData_tunl.txt: CsI-Na quenching factor data points from TUNL experiment shown in publication.

	coherent_parameters.yaml: YAML file with entries corresponding to relevant bits of information which can be expressed as single numbers.
